title: Cyclic Tasks
files:
  - em.prog:em.examples.basic/Ex13_TickerP.em.ts
  - em.core:em.utils/TickerMgr.em.ts
  - .assets/img-101-07-01.png

steps:

  - cmds:
      - view 3
    text: |

      {[ht,$start] Home}

      This tour examines the {[cu]TickerP} program, which winks `AppLed` [1.0&thinsp;s] _and_ `SysLed` [1.5&thinsp;s] at different rates.

      Looking at the {[cu]TickerP} signal capture, aligned wakeups cause each wink to start at precise intervals from reset.

      In cases where these intervals coincide (such as +3&thinsp;s mark), `AppLed`{[bm,A]} and `SysLed`{[bm,S]} wink in succession.

      This tour also introduces {[cu]TickerMgr} &ndash; yet another instance of the **EMS** _object-factory_ design pattern



  - cmds:
      - open 1
      - mark 1 A 10
      - mark 1 B 13
      - mark 1 C 18
    focus: [1,1]
    text: |

      {[ht,$details]%[cu]TickerP% &ndash; Details}
 
